From 9faa298823b28b8d8f841092f0e21c19fee4d082 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude (sandbox)" <claude@sandbox.local>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 08:39:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] EventV1/OutcomeV1: stamped events, durable outcome
 obligations, live kernel

The governance kernel was solid and judging nothing real: every production
caller of make_episode/judge_episode was a test, and the live path scored
calls down a parallel route on numbers whose origin it had forgotten. This
connects real (labelled) events to the kernel and gives outcomes that mature
after the decision a record of their own.

EventV1 (event_v1.py)
  One observed fact, stamped verified / attested / estimated. An estimate
  that will not name its method does not validate -- an unlabelled estimate
  is indistinguishable from a measurement, which is the record an auditor
  cannot accept. assemble_episode routes by stamp: verified and estimated
  land in Episode.actual, attested lands in Episode.actor_report, so
  episode.py's existing actor-distrust cross-check starts working on
  ingested events with no change to episode.py at all. Absolute occurred_at
  / observed_at replace offsets from an assumed start time.

OutcomeV1 (outcome_v1.py)
  Carries The Provenance Rule as its module docstring. Two records, two
  lifespans: the decision closes permanently, the obligation is separate and
  durable. OPEN / RESOLVED / ABANDONED with bounded typed reason
  vocabularies -- no flat indeterminate flag. "Overdue" is arithmetic on
  opened_at/expected_by, never a stored column somebody can set to False.
  MaturationRule parses and emits the declaration string that hashes into
  the decision row. to_cohort_decision is the return path C2 dimension 4 has
  been structurally waiting for, and it refuses to coerce an unresolved or
  genuinely-ambiguous outcome into a bool.

Linkage, one-directional
  The decision row carries the maturation rule in force at decision time
  (canonical_fields.OPTIONAL_HASHED_FIELDS -- the documented one-line
  addition). Knowable at decision time, so it hashes in immediately and
  never changes. The obligation points back at the decision's current_hash;
  the decision points at nothing, which is what lets it close forever.

Twin (own table, own vocabulary)
  obligation_ledger: append-only, hash-chained per replica, same shape as
  custody_log. The twin DERIVES the open set from the decision feed itself
  rather than being told, so an operator cannot suppress an obligation
  without suppressing the decision (already MISSING on the existing
  cross-check). The declaration and decided_at ship in the clear so
  derivation works without decryption authority; a horizon measured from
  arrival would let a slow shipper stretch every deadline. Deliberately not
  replica_entries and not twin_detector's verdicts -- its PENDING means
  "inside the transport SLA" and its EXTRA means "wiped".

outcome_harm_event record kind
  The governance exception to "per-decision outcome is business reporting".
  A defaulted loan on a calibrated model is expected loss; a denial reversed
  on appeal establishes that the PROCESS failed. Not a decision_supersession
  -- a supersession replaces an output, a harm event may have no replacement
  at all and may be discovered by someone with no authority to supersede
  anything. Filing both under one kind leaves an examiner unable to count
  either.

Live path (production_harness)
  Every call now assembles a validated Episode from stamped events and runs
  judge_episode. Additive on purpose: quality_score still drives behaviour
  and the kernel's verdict is recorded alongside it and cross-checked, so a
  disagreement becomes an observable ledger fact instead of an assumption.
  The route heuristic and the 0.1/0.5/0.4 wait split are NOT fixed here --
  they now travel as estimated with the derivation named.

Two defects found and fixed
  * verify_chain reconstructs canonical forms from its own column list and
    did not select outcome_obligation -- every row carrying one would have
    failed its own verification.
  * verify_chain had no outcome_harm_event branch, so a harm event would
    fall through to the legacy path. A new record kind is not done until all
    three recompute sites agree (writer, verify_chain, twin_custody).

event_v1 and outcome_v1 join cassette_forensics._GOVERNANCE_CODE_MODULES --
same class as episode.py, they define what the system accepts as a fact.
Moved code hash => new version under binding enforcement: IVR 2.0.1->2.0.2,
banking 2.0.2->2.0.3. Neither cassette enables the new capability; an IVR
call's outcome is settled at hangup and it owes nothing later.

544 passed / 6 skipped (442 baseline + 102 new) twice back-to-back from a
clean ledger; ruff clean; bandit introduces no new findings.
